hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1103","Chapter on the dislike of taking copies of the Qur'an into enemy land, 1142 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Malik informed me, from Nafi', from Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade travelling with the Qur'an to enemy land, fearing the enemy would seize it."
